Gecko codes online between two Melee-NX-NetPlay builds, and the smoother time sync developer aid (Melee-NX-NetPlay 0.4.8).
melee-unlocked's Gecko code messages (host/gecko_online.h: offer, answer, lock; upstream keeps them off, kOnlineCodes) travel as
NP_MSG_NX_GECKO (0xD3) to a peer whose build message has flag 0x40 (its player turned Gecko codes online on); the session rules
(gecko_session.cpp) run in the program (frontend/src/features/gecko.cpp) behind weak mu_net_gecko_* hooks: a Direct 1v1 only, the
lock just before every selection on the same ordered queue, the decision at the match's first frame from both locks. Against
Slippi Dolphin, melee-unlocked or a build without it: no flag, nothing sent. MELEE_SYNC_SMOOTH=1 (upstream's developer aid):
time sync's speed correction from 2 ms, this side's pacing only. Applied by ../net_sources.sh after net-0012 (and net-0013).
